Section 2(1) of the Nigerian Copyright Act 2022 lists the types of works that are eligible for copyright protection. However, there is no Section 2(1)(g) in the Act as you provided. The list in Section 2(1) includes:

(a) literary works;
(b) musical works;
(c) artistic works;
(d) audiovisual works;
(e) sound recordings; and
(f) broadcasts.

If you are looking for additional categories or specific provisions, please check the text of the Act for any updates or amendments that may not be reflected in the provided extracts. As it stands, the current list of eligible works for copyright under Section 2(1) does not include a (g) category.
